To handle cache invalidation, we use a timestamp to mark when the cache entry was last updated. When the cache is accessed again, we check if the timestamp has changed. If it has, we remove the key from the cache.

This approach ensures that cache invalidation is handled correctly, even if the cache is accessed concurrently by multiple clients.

